To get the correct team for a kill, many cases should be considered to make the game
feel fair.

Cases:
    A player kills a ball directly
    A player shoots a ball
    A player kills a ball with a roped ball
    A player hits a ball into another player
    Any combination, i.e hits a roped ball into a ball which kills a player

Rules:
    When a neutral ball is hit by another faster moving ball, it takes the team of
    that ball temperarily. /


    A neutral ball with no temporary team will always be overwritten. /


    A neutral ball will take the temporary team of another neutral ball,
    but will not hold the team longer than the other ball. /


    A player ball will hold a temporary team for a shorter length of time than a neutral  /


    A bullet will always hold the team of the ball that shot it. /


    A bullets act the same as balls. /


    When a ball is pulled by a rope, the force is treated like a collision and the
    ball's team will change. 


pseudocode:
    tempTeam is stored as a table
    [
        team,
        tick that the team changed
    ]

    //Returns the tick the team changed, or the current tick if no tempTeam exists
    function getTeam(ball)
        tempLength = 120
        if playerBalls:has(ball) then tempLength = 30 endif

        if tick - ball.tempTeam[2] < tempLength then 
            return [ball.tempTeam[1],ball.tempTeam[2]] 
        endif

        return [ball.innateTeam,tick]
    endfunction

    aggressor = faster ball, defender = slower ball.
    if the speeds are too similar, neither changes team

    //If the aggressor is neutral, its team changes, as neutral balls always change team.
    //Else, the defender always changes team to the aggressors team 
    //Takes aggressorTeam to manually overwrite the tempTeam
    procedure teamChange(aggressor,defender,aggressorTeam)
        if aggressorTeam == nil then aggressorTeam = getTeam(aggressor) endif

        if aggressorTeam == neutral then 
            aggressor.tempTeam = getTeam(defender) 
            return 
        endif
        defender.tempTeam = aggressorTeam
    endprocedure

    //setting the innate team of bullets to the player's team,
    //as bullets are destroyed on collision, the tempTeam will not interfere.
    class ball
        ...
        public procedure shoot(angle,velocity)
            ...
            nBall.innateTeam = innateTeam
        endprocedure
        ...
    endclass


    //Changes to updateRopes to allow for the correct team to be calculated
    class World
        ...
        public procedure updateRopes()
            ...
            procedure process(balls,centre,length,elasticity)
                ...
                speed1 = Util:findDistance(ball1.vx,ball1.vy)
                speed2 = Util:findDistance(ball2.vx,ball2.vy)
                
                //Use the innate team rather than possibility of temp team, as ropes
                //always come from the innate player team
                if speed1 >= speed2 then teamChange(ball1,ball2,ball1.innateTeam) endif
                if speed2 > speed1 then  teamChange(ball2,ball1,ball2.innateTeam) endif
                ...
            endprocedure
            ...
        endprocedure
        ...
    endclass